<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντεῖπον</span></b> , aor. 2 without any
			pres. (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντερῶ, ἀντιλέγω,
			ἀνταγορεύω</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speak against</i> or <i>in answer, gainsay,</i> c. dat.,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				999
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινὶ δεομένῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.136
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲν ἀντειπεῖν ἔχω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					51
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρός τινα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.3.3
			</span></i>; <i>oppose,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Thg.</u>
				131a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὑπέρ τινος</span>
			<i>speak</i> in one's defence, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				545
			</span></i>: c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἔπος</span>
			<i>utter</i> a word <i>of contradiction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1391
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύο λόγω περὶ τῶν αὐτῶν
				ἀντειπεῖν</span>
			<i>speak on both sides of</i> a question, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				10.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τούτῳ ἂν δίκαιον λόγον ἀντείποιμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					28b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶς ἀ. τινά</span>
			<i>malign</i> him <i>in turn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1053
			</span></i>.</div>
